config KFEAT_RTC
    bool "RTC (Real Time Clock) class support"
    default y
    help
      Build the real-time clock class (subsys-rtc) and its boot wall-clock
      seeding service. The class is a consumer contract; an actual clock
      comes from one of the KFEAT_DRIVER_RTC_* backends. Without a backend
      the class stays empty and the wall clock keeps its epoch base.

config KFEAT_DISPLAY
    bool "Display Driver Support"
    default y
    help
      Enable display driver support (virtio-gpu, fbdevice, etc).

config KFEAT_INPUT
    bool "Input Driver Support"
    default y
    help
      Enable input driver support (virtio-input, inputdev, etc).

config KFEAT_CHAR
    bool "Character Driver Support"
    default y
    help
      Enable runtime character device support. This covers devices that are
      exposed after early boot handoff or through the unified driver pipeline.
endmenu   # Device Drivers Features

