config KFEAT_DRIVER_RTC_GOLDFISH
    bool "Goldfish RTC driver"
    depends on KFEAT_RTC && ARCH_RISCV64
    default y if MACHINE_RISCV64_QEMU
    help
      Goldfish virtual RTC driver (`google,goldfish-rtc`) on the
      driver-core model.

config KFEAT_DRIVER_RTC_CMOS
    bool "CMOS RTC driver"
    depends on KFEAT_RTC && ARCH_X86_64
    default y if MACHINE_X86_64_QEMU
    help
      PC-compatible CMOS clock driver on the driver-core model. X86 has no
      firmware description, so the composition root enumerates a
      board-static `rtc-cmos` device carrying the fixed 0x70/0x71 port
      pair.

config KFEAT_DRIVER_RTC_LS7A
    bool "LS7A RTC driver"
    depends on KFEAT_RTC && ARCH_LOONGARCH64
    default y if MACHINE_LOONGARCH64_QEMU
    help
      Loongson LS7A TOY-counter RTC driver on the driver-core model.
      Claims the device-tree node when present; otherwise the composition
      root enumerates a board-static `rtc-ls7a` device from RTC_PADDR.

config KFEAT_MMC
    bool "MMC/SD subsystem (mmc core + card bus)"
    help
      Build the MMC/SD subsystem (subsys-mmc): the host contract, the mmc
      card bus and the SD protocol core. A storage stack needs one of the
      KFEAT_DRIVER_MMC_* host backends plus KFEAT_DRIVER_MMC_BLOCK.

config KFEAT_DRIVER_MMC_BLOCK
    bool "MMC block device (mmc_blk)"
    depends on KFEAT_MMC
    help
      The card-bus consumer publishing discovered SD cards as block
      devices (Gendisk major 179) into the block class.

config MMC_MULTIBLOCK
    bool "MMC multi-block reads (CMD18 + auto-stop)"
    depends on KFEAT_DRIVER_MMC_BLOCK
    default y
    help
      Read a multi-block request with one CMD18 instead of one CMD17 per
      block. Cheaper per byte, but the auto-stop path streams blocks
      back-to-back: on a polled (PIO) data path a drain loop that loses the
      CPU long enough overruns the FIFO. The consumer therefore latches
      this off after the first failed multi-block transfer and keeps going
      with per-block reads, so the switch only decides the first attempt.

config KFEAT_DRIVER_MMC_DWMMC_ROCKCHIP
    bool "DesignWare MMC host driver (Rockchip)"
    depends on KFEAT_MMC && ARCH_AARCH64
    help
      DW MSHC host driver (dw_mmc-rockchip shape) for RK3588-class SD
      controllers: MMIO + FIFO-polled PIO data path, card detection onto
      the mmc card bus. The CIU input rate is a board fact (MMC_CIU_HZ)
      and the card-clock ceiling is a board fact (MMC_MAX_CARD_HZ) — the
      SD clock domain sits behind the firmware and is left configured by
      the boot stages.

config MMC_CIU_HZ
    hex "MMC CIU input clock rate (Hz)"
    depends on KFEAT_DRIVER_MMC_DWMMC_ROCKCHIP
    default 0x2FAF080
    help
      The CIU input clock feeding the DWMMC internal divider (the rate
      the firmware/boot stages configured for the SD clock domain). The
      driver divides this down for 400 kHz init, 25 MHz default speed
      and 50 MHz high speed; it never reprograms the source.

config MMC_4BIT
    bool "MMC 4-bit bus support"
    depends on KFEAT_DRIVER_MMC_DWMMC_ROCKCHIP
    default y
    help
      Advertise the controller's DAT1..DAT3 lines to the SD core. Unset this
      to keep every card in 1-bit mode: the bring-up switch for a slot whose
      wide data lines do not reach the controller (every data phase then
      fails with a start-bit error while commands stay healthy).

config MMC_MAX_CARD_HZ
    hex "MMC card clock ceiling (Hz)"
    depends on KFEAT_DRIVER_MMC_DWMMC_ROCKCHIP
    default 0x2FAF080
    help
      Upper bound for the card clock the host programs, applied to every
      set_ios request (the DT max-frequency caps it further; whichever is
      lower wins). 0 disables the cap.

      This is the bring-up knob for the divider arithmetic: because the
      source rate is unmeasurable (MMC_CIU_HZ is an assumption), a board
      that mis-samples at the nominal mode rate lowers this instead of
      guessing a new source rate. If a lower ceiling makes the data phases
      pass, the effective source rate was higher than MMC_CIU_HZ claims.


config KFEAT_DRIVER_CLK_SCMI
    bool "SCMI clock provider driver"
    depends on ARCH_AARCH64
    help
      SCMI clock-domain provider over an SMC-dispatched SMT channel
      (clk-scmi shape). RK3588 keeps the SD controller clocks behind the
      EL3 SCMI agent; without this provider their consumers defer.

config SCMI_SMC_ID
    hex "SCMI SMC function id"
    depends on KFEAT_DRIVER_CLK_SCMI
    default 0x82000010
    help
      SMCCC function identifier for the SCMI SMC transport (DT
      `arm,smc-id` on the `scmi` node; the protocol child cannot carry
      it, so the board fact lands here).

config SCMI_SHMEM_PADDR
    hex "SCMI SMT shared memory base address"
    depends on KFEAT_DRIVER_CLK_SCMI
    default 0x10f000
    help
      Physical base of the SMT shared-memory channel (DT `scmi_shmem`
      node; 0x100 bytes). Mapped through the device resource door.

